<header><p class="st-kicker">tribal confederation · Iberia</p><h1 class="st-title">Olcades</h1><p class="st-meta">400 BCE – 221 BCE (approx.) · capital Althaia</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A people of the southern Meseta whose capital Althaia was Hannibal's first conquest as commander in Iberia, in 221 BCE.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The Olcades lived in the upper <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guadiana">Guadiana</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jucar">Júcar</a> region of the southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/meseta-central">Meseta</a>, probably in modern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cuenca-spain">Cuenca</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ciudad-real">Ciudad Real</a>. Their origins are obscure, and ancient sources mention them only in connection with the Carthaginian campaigns.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Nothing is known of their institutions beyond their capital, which <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/polybius">Polybius</a> calls Althaia and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/livy">Livy</a> Cartala, and their wealth in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cattle">cattle</a> and grain.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>In 221 BCE <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hannibal">Hannibal</a> attacked them, took Althaia and forced them to pay tribute. The next year Olcadian refugees joined the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/carpetani">Carpetani</a> and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/vaccaei">Vaccaei</a> against him at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tagus">Tagus</a> and were defeated. They vanish from the record after this, absorbed into <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/barcid-iberia">Barcid Iberia</a> and later <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hispania">Roman Hispania</a>.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="tribal confederation, 400 BCE – 221 BCE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><ellipse cx="44" cy="56" rx="16" ry="24"/><path d="M44 34 V78"/><path d="M68 20 V84"/><path d="M68 20 L63 30 H73 Z"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">tribal confederation</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Iberia</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:51.74%;width:3.56%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>400 BCE – 221 BCE (approx.)</dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>tribal confederation</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>tribal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Althaia</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd>Spain</dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Olcadians</dd></dl></aside></div>

